<title>USA: U.S. Jan business inventories rose 0.1 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. Jan business inventories rose 0.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Commerce Department said U.S. January business inventories rose 0.1 percent after falling 0.1 percent in December. It said January business sales rose 1.2 percent after falling a revised 0.2 percent in December.</p>
<p>The following lists business inventories and sales by sector, in billions of dollars, seasonally adjusted:</p>
<p>    INVENTORIES:  January  December----(Prev)   November</p>
<p> Total Business  1,011.11  1,009.74  1,009.46  1,010.92</p>
<p> Durable Goods     607.69    606.89    607.43    608.93</p>
<p> NonDurable Goods  403.42    402.85    402.04    401.98</p>
<p>    INVENTORIES:  January  December---(Prev)    November</p>
<p> Manufacturers     438.15   437.92    438.17     439.37</p>
<p> Retailers	   312.16   313.71    314.96     313.62</p>
<p> --Auto Dealers     87.48    88.21     88.76</p>
<p> Wholesalers	 260.80   258.11    256.34     257.93</p>
<p>    SALES:	  January  December---(Prev)    November</p>
<p> Total Business    735.93   727.43    727.76     728.80</p>
<p> Durable Goods     361.70   357.90    357.64     359.30</p>
<p> NonDurable Goods  374.23   369.53    370.12     369.51</p>
<p>    SALES:	  January  December---(Prev)    November</p>
<p> Manufacturers     318.69   315.28    315.56     317.55</p>
<p> Retailers	   211.46   208.32    207.87     207.32</p>
<p> --Auto Dealers     52.10    51.10     50.10</p>
<p> Wholesalers	 205.79   203.84    204.34     203.93</p>
<p> Inventory-To-    January  December---(Prev)    November</p>
<p>  Sales Ratio	  1.37     1.39	1.39	 1.39</p>
<p>The 1.37 inventory-to-sales ratio in January was the lowest since the department began compiling comparable data in January 1982. The inventory-to-sales ratio is a measure of how long it would take to sell existing stocks at the current pace.</p>
<p>The department revised December business sales from the previously reported 0.1 percent drop.</p>
